+++ b/apps/claude-code-worker/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,68 @@
+# Claude Code worker
+
+Deployment, account provisioning and rollback steps: [DEPLOYMENT.md](./DEPLOYMENT.md).
+
+Internal ordinary-assistant executor. Each instance must be assigned to exactly
+one LobeHub user and run in its own non-root container with separate home,
+Claude configuration, workspace, and state volumes. The state volume is mandatory: it retains event
+receipts across restarts. Do not share these volumes between users or workers.
+
+Each LobeHub turn starts a new official CLI process with a fresh session ID and
+the full context prepared by LobeHub. The ordinary-assistant mode never uses
+`--resume` or saves a cross-turn CLI session mapping. Official login and workspace
+files persist in the user's volumes; tool loops continue within the active run.
+The launcher fixes `CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AUTO_MEMORY=1`, so Claude's automatic
+memory files are neither loaded nor created. Explicit workspace files and
+`CLAUDE.md` remain available; LobeHub prepares the current user-memory context.
+
+Build from the repository root using `apps/claude-code-worker/Dockerfile` and set
+`LOBEHUB_BUILD_REVISION` to the checked-out commit. The image pins Claude Code;
+startup checks its version before accepting model work. Keep the main app and
+worker build revisions in the deployment record.
+
+Required configuration:
+
+| Variable                    | Meaning                                               |
+| --------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |
+| `LOBEHUB_WORKER_SERVER_URL` | Trusted LobeHub base URL; HTTPS across hosts          |
+| `LOBEHUB_WORKER_ID`         | Administrator-assigned worker binding                 |
+| `LOBEHUB_WORKER_TOKEN_FILE` | Read-only file containing this worker's service token |
+
+The service token is distinct from Claude credentials. It is used only for the
+internal worker protocol and is never passed to the CLI environment. The server
+must bind that token to this exact worker and user. Avoid putting the token in
+the container environment or command line.
+
+An administrator provisions the environment, then the user runs the official
+`claude auth login` in a terminal inside their assigned container, as user
+`10001:10001`, with `HOME=/home/claude` and
+`CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/home/claude/.claude`. The official program owns subscription
+credentials and refresh. The worker reports only the login category, CLI version,
+and official model catalog. It does not return account names or Claude tokens.
+
+Do not supply Anthropic/API provider credentials, proxy endpoints, Docker socket,
+host directories, or another user's volumes. The CLI subprocess receives only
+the explicit safe runtime environment. Its local command/file tools are scoped
+by container isolation. Drop Linux capabilities, enable `no-new-privileges`,
+and apply memory/CPU limits in deployment. Only trusted administrators should
+control the server URL, token file, image, and mounted volumes.
+
+The worker exposes no public port. Its operation-specific MCP listener binds
+loopback. `/claim` is the authoritative global queue, and the worker executes
+one claimed run at a time. The durable journal is delivered by sequence; retries
+never rerun the CLI. A saved active run becomes interrupted after restart. A
+lease expiry or cancellation terminates the CLI process group with escalation.
+Pending LobeHub tools await their original receipt ID until real completion.
+The worker begins shutdown five seconds before its last confirmed lease expires,
+allowing forced process termination before another worker is admitted. If a run
+has been removed and its receipts return 404 or 410, recovery preserves its full
+journal under `state/quarantine/` for administrator inspection and proceeds with
+other runs. Authentication and transport failures still retain the active journal.
+
+For rollback disable the server entry and stop admission, then stop the worker
+and restore the previous app image. Preserve all four per-user volumes. Do not
+delete login data or journals to clear an interrupted task.
+
+The local tests cover protocol, isolation and recovery boundaries. Live official
+login, two-user isolation, browser/mobile interactions, and Docker resource
+limits require the staged deployment acceptance suite before enabling users.
diff --git a/apps/claude-code-worker/__tests__/startup.integration.test.ts b/apps/claude-code-worker/__tests__/startup.integration.test.ts
